// wskill standard library — prelude.
//
// The public entry point is `wskill.wcl`, which a wskill root document opts
// into with `import <wskill.wcl>`; that imports this file, which pulls in
// every schema part. The parts are embedded in the binary and resolved through
// the registry (see `crates/wcl_wskill/src/stdlib.rs`); the angle-bracket
// paths are importer-relative, so `import <schema.wcl>` here resolves to
// `wskill/schema.wcl`.
//
// Ordering does not matter — names resolve across every imported file.
//
// The two optional views' schemas ship unconditionally: declaring the
// `lesson` / `presentation` block types costs a wskill nothing until it
// authors one, and the gathered lists stay empty. A view SHIPS when the
// wskill declares its `artifact` and renders the matching projection.
//
// `EntityKind` and `ArtifactKind` are deliberately NOT here: they are the
// topic-OWNED vocabularies, and every wskill keeps its own hand-editable
// `schema/kinds.wcl` declaring them in this same namespace.

namespace wcl.wskill

import <schema.wcl>           // the base wskill data model + the root @document
import <presentation.wcl>     // optional view: the topic-overview slide deck
import <training.wcl>         // optional view: the hands-on tutorial course
